{"data": [{"broadcast_id": "Brp2ybdlij", "broadcast_date": "2004-07-30", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1660, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761098, "segment_id": "08oGekwbgA", "segment_broadcast_id": "Brp2ybdlij", "segment_title": "Preview/Introduction Dan Rather (New York)", "segment_description": "NOTE - Local weather bulletin on screen from 5:41:10 to 5:42:10.", "segment_duration": 40, "segment_type_id": 1, "segment_start_time": "63000.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761098, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "Preview", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "Brp2ybdlij", "broadcast_date": "2004-07-30", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1660, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761098, "segment_id": "35t42N3U7H", "segment_broadcast_id": "Brp2ybdlij", "segment_title": "Campaign 04 / Bush vs. Kerry", "segment_description": "(Studio: Dan Rather) Report introduced. \n (Scranton, Pennsylvania: Jim Axelrod) The campaign tour of Democratic candidates Senators John Kerry & John Edwards featured; map shown of the \u201cBelieve in America\u201d bus tour; scenes shown of Edwards and wife Elizabeth celebrating their anniversary at Wendy\u2019s restaurant in Newburg, New York; details given about the post-convention bounce, or the momentum created by winning undecided voters. [KERRY \u2013 campaigns.] [Scranton, Pennsylvania, VOTER \u2013 comments.] [Kerry press secretary David WADE&#134;, Bush-Cheney press secretary Terry HOLT&#134;- offer differing opinions on the bounce.] \n (Studio: Dan Rather) Report introduced. \n (Cleveland: John Roberts) President Bush\u2019s campaign trip through battleground states featured. [BUSH \u2013 criticizes Kerry; states he agrees with the 9/11 Commission\u2019s assessment of homeland security.] [Republican pollster Frank LUNTZ&#134;- says the candidate that seems to be able to implement the recommendations {of the 9/11 Commission} will win the swing voters.] The White House prediction of the federal deficit cited.", "segment_duration": 290, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63040.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761099, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "Brp2ybdlij", "broadcast_date": "2004-07-30", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1660, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761098, "segment_id": "FtrC1DFFTX", "segment_broadcast_id": "Brp2ybdlij", "segment_title": "September 11 / Commission Report / Recommendations", "segment_description": "(Studio: Dan Rather) Senator John Kerry\u2019s declaration that Al Qaeda leader Osama bin Laden should be tried for murder in American courts when he is caught, and his embracing of the 9/11 Commission\u2019s recommendations for national security noted. \n (Washington: Bob Orr) The pressure on President Bush & Congress to immediately implement the commission\u2019s recommendations featured; details given of uncertainty over how far Bush or Congress will go towards implementing the major recommendations: the creation of a national counterterrorism center and a national intelligence director. [In Michigan, BUSH \u2013 cites security improvements already in place.] [9/11 Commission vice chairman Lee HAMILTON&#134;- comments on the need for somebody to be \u201creally in charge.\u201d] [Commission chairman Thomas KEAN&#134;- says the present system is unacceptable and doesn\u2019t work.] [Senator Joseph LIEBERMAN&#134;- says we cannot let another attack succeed because of our own inaction.]", "segment_duration": 130, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63330.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761100, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "Brp2ybdlij", "broadcast_date": "2004-07-30", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1660, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761098, "segment_id": "qYY5Nt0ecT", "segment_broadcast_id": "Brp2ybdlij", "segment_title": "Iraq / Unrest", "segment_description": "(Studio: Dan Rather) NATO\u2019s agreement to assist training Iraqi security forces reported.   (Baghdad: Kimberly Dozier) The all-night gunfight between insurgents and US Marines, who were targeting followers of Abu Mussab al-Zarqawi, in Fallujah, Iraq, reviewed; scenes shown from the town; details given of the Iraqi government\u2019s fight against Zarqawi. [Iraqi prime minister\u2019s spokesperson Georges SADA&#134;- says we are asking our friends to help us.] [In Iraq, Secretary of State Colin POWELL \u2013 says we are here as guests to help you until you can provide for your own security.] The proposal from Saudi Arabia for an Arab force to help secure Iraq mentioned.   (Studio: Dan Rather) The results of a government audit of funds spent on Iraq cited.", "segment_duration": 150, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63460.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761101, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "Brp2ybdlij", "broadcast_date": "2004-07-30", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1660, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761098, "segment_id": "rpBPuzyNT7", "segment_broadcast_id": "Brp2ybdlij", "segment_title": "Upcoming Items; fallen soldier Army S/Sgt. Paul Neff, II&#134<!-- spelling on screen --> profiled. (Studio: Dan Rather)", "segment_description": "null", "segment_duration": 50, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63610.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761102, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "Brp2ybdlij", "broadcast_date": "2004-07-30", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1660, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761098, "segment_id": "umLQsS34iT", "segment_broadcast_id": "Brp2ybdlij", "segment_title": "(Commercial: Hyundai; Metamucil; Thompson\u2019s Water Seal; Excellence; Maalox; Bristol-Myers Squibb Co.; York.)", "segment_description": "null", "segment_duration": 150, "segment_type_id": 3, "segment_start_time": "63660.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761103, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "Commercial", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "Brp2ybdlij", "broadcast_date": "2004-07-30", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1660, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761098, "segment_id": "lACdyeLwd9", "segment_broadcast_id": "Brp2ybdlij", "segment_title": "Inside Story (Uzbekistan)", "segment_description": "(Studio: Dan Rather) Islamic militants\u2019 claim of responsibility for suicide attacks on US & Israeli embassies in Uzbekistan noted; scenes shown from Tashkent. \n (London: Sheila MacVicar) Uzbekistan\u2019s halting progress towards democracy, despite an alliance with the US that is essential to operations in Afghanistan, featured; details given of claims of torture and oppression by the government; scenes shown from a US military base. [US Air Force Col. Tim VINING&#134;- says they were the first country after 9/11 to open up for us to stage humanitarian relief.] [US base commander Lt. Col. Neal KEMP&#134;- comments on the relative safety of the air base.] [Human Rights Watch Allison GILL&#134;- comments on Uzbekistan\u2019s poor human rights record.] [Uzbek Foreign Minister Sodiq SAFAYEV&#134;- comments on the government\u2019s fight against terror.]", "segment_duration": 180, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63810.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761104, "network_name": "CBS", "broadcast_type_name": "Evening News", "segment_type_name": "News", "segment_contributors_with_roles": null, "broadcast_contributors_with_roles": null, "topic_names": null, "location_names": null}, {"broadcast_id": "Brp2ybdlij", "broadcast_date": "2004-07-30", "broadcast_start_time": "63000.0", "network": 2, "distributor": 9, "broadcast_title": "CBS Evening News", "broadcast_type_id": 1, "broadcast_duration": 1660, "broadcast_description": null, "legacy_broadcast_id": 761098, "segment_id": "kjW6Ghjc7R", "segment_broadcast_id": "Brp2ybdlij", "segment_title": "Belgium / Gas Explosion", "segment_description": "(Studio: Dan Rather) A massive natural gas explosion in Belgium reported; scenes shown from Ghislenghien.", "segment_duration": 10, "segment_type_id": 2, "segment_start_time": "63990.0", "legacy_segment_id": 761105, "network_name": "CBS", "broa